      "title": "Analog Computation with Waves",
      "gist": "Like physical analog computers, overlapping brain waves can add, cancel, and combine continuously and in parallel, letting the brain compute efficiently without discrete digital steps.",
      "question": "Analog computation — how could interacting brain waves perform actual computation rather than merely organizing activity? (a worked example)",
      "sourceHeading": "Analog Computation with Waves"
    },
